{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513187-less-harmful-feeding-debates-round-2","id":1513187,"title":"\"Less harmful feeding\" debates, round 2","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-29T04:31:00-07:00","id":1513187,"title":"\"Less harmful feeding\" debates, round 2","content":"The topic of feeding and ethics thereof returned, this time going down stranger lines and alternatives to a (living) human-based diet. So, out of curiosity about the rest of the fandom, what's everyone's thoughts on (or ever overlooked alternatives to) following a strict diet of:<br /> <b>A) Carrion</b>. Blood from butchers and abattoirs, sucking up what blood you can get from roadkill and other dead animals, rejected blood donations, blood drained from an already dead body during embalming.<br /> If you do something to the drain, you can divert the drained blood to vampires for redistribution. The Tremere can probably preserve/improve the blood, if you're willing to trust them not to do anything else with it.<br /> <br /> \u2022Counterarguments against this one are that there are rules that say vampires need to feed from living humans eventually.<br /> Counterarguments were that those rules are obscure and optional, unless you're playing with V5's hunger system, so they can be dismissed by default.<br /> <i>\u2022 Somebody</i> is going to see a potential market in this, get a stranglehold on the market and ensure that the only way you can get your blood within hunting is by sucking up to them and possibly doing crime on their orders. Vampire politics gets into everything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>B) Cannibalism</b>. If vampires don't count as people, is it ok to hunt them instead? You don't have to diablerise them or kill them, and if you borrow a bit from V5 then if you avoid drinking it right out of the vein it doesn't form a blood bond.<br /> (I personally will treat this the same as I treat feeding on humans)<br /> <br /> Counterargument:<br /> Vampires are sapient and thus count as people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>C) Necromancy</b>. Syphon ambient entropic energy. Eat spectres. Make a deal with an usurer to convert pathos for you. etc<br /> <br /> Counterarguments:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u2022 &quot;Dealing with the Underworld is playing with fire, in a way.&quot; - &quot;So is being a vampire.&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u2022 Many will not take kindly to you making their skinlands business more difficult by strengthening the Shroud.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u2022 Considering the Hivemind, how are the local Spectres and Shadows going to respond to you actively hunting them? Besides that, it feels like there should be side effects to sucking up something so thoroughly tainted with Oblivion.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u2022 Is dealing with a vampire technically a breach of the Dictum Mortum, since they've already died?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u2022 Is feeding from wraiths better than feeding on the living? Especially as wraiths may just be the memory of people instead of actual people (cue reprise of &quot;what defines personhood?&quot; and a loop back to &quot;is eating vamps acceptable&quot;) Or is siphoning off a deceased soul - even consensually - on the same dangerous ground as drinking from a consenting mortal.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u2022 &quot;But there's always the chance that, in making a deal for a pathos to vitae conversation, you're going to have do something just as bad as you'd do in normal vamp deals. Stygia is, frankly, just as bad or maybe worse than the Cam.&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">&quot;Are they really worse though?&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">&quot;They build their houses with bricks made of the eternally weeping souls of their neighbours and have open slave markets.&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">&quot;Vampires don't need to purchase slaves, they can just make them for free. And the only thing keeping society enmasse from building furniture out of impudent fledglings is because it's a Masquerade breach and not everyone has access to Vicissitude.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">And then everything got sidetracked into a debate about the Stygian Hierarchy vs the Ivory Tower.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}